WEBVTT

00:01:15.522 --> 00:01:16.757
Walter here,
I'm at Market Plaza.

00:01:16.757 --> 00:01:18.358
Little Giant
Walter here,
I'm at Market Plaza.

00:01:18.358 --> 00:01:19.026
Little Giant

00:01:19.026 --> 00:01:20.360
Little Giant
All except Tonio and Walter,
go check outside the plaza.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:21.918
All except Tonio and Walter,
go check outside the plaza.

00:01:22.629 --> 00:01:23.330
Tonio here.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:24.456
I found them.

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:29.469
I'm sure it's Rosa Raine.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.673
And the one standing next
to her is Frederick Hoffman?

00:01:32.673 --> 00:01:33.273
Yes.

00:01:33.273 --> 00:01:35.901
He officially joined
as a member recently.

00:01:36.243 --> 00:01:38.734
Anyway, he's only a rookie.

00:01:39.079 --> 00:01:40.808
Okay, continue trailing them.

00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:44.284
Wait, Tonio!

00:01:44.284 --> 00:01:45.546
Turn the camera back!

00:01:48.422 --> 00:01:51.224
A stranger is approaching Rosa.

00:01:51.224 --> 00:01:52.125
Is he one of them?

00:01:52.125 --> 00:01:53.827
Never seen him in the RAF.

00:01:53.827 --> 00:01:55.556
Then, could he be in
the same business?

00:01:56.463 --> 00:01:58.624
He doesn't seem
like a professional.

00:01:59.132 --> 00:02:00.434
Walter, Tonio...

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.202
...we'll call it off for today.

00:02:02.202 --> 00:02:03.236
But...

00:02:03.236 --> 00:02:04.371
We have no choice.

00:02:04.371 --> 00:02:08.705
It's better then having that
stranger ruin our plan.

00:02:09.976 --> 00:02:11.244
Perfect.

00:02:11.244 --> 00:02:14.042
Let's invite him for tea.

00:02:21.088 --> 00:02:25.184
Dusseldorf, Germany

00:02:28.328 --> 00:02:29.863
A pointer?

00:02:29.863 --> 00:02:30.564
Yes.

00:02:30.564 --> 00:02:32.794
The best hunting
dog you can find.

00:02:32.999 --> 00:02:34.801
He creeps in without a sound...

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:37.571
...and he'll keep pointing
at the prey for hours.

00:02:37.571 --> 00:02:39.906
He won't bark or attack.

00:02:39.906 --> 00:02:42.306
Just keeps watching the prey.

00:02:42.609 --> 00:02:44.577
Just like us.

00:02:45.178 --> 00:02:47.373
Anyway, please take a seat.

00:02:52.686 --> 00:02:55.722
So, who are you?

00:02:55.722 --> 00:02:58.555
Why are you interfering
with our work?

00:02:58.759 --> 00:03:00.021
Interfering?!

00:03:00.327 --> 00:03:01.555
Right...

00:03:02.796 --> 00:03:04.024
Here you are.

00:03:04.765 --> 00:03:06.867
Insurance Investigator.

00:03:06.867 --> 00:03:09.028
Taichi Hiraga Keaton.

00:03:09.736 --> 00:03:11.738
So you're an op?

00:03:11.738 --> 00:03:12.572
Yes.

00:03:12.572 --> 00:03:14.374
Lloyd's of London has asked me...

00:03:14.374 --> 00:03:16.274
...to investigate Rosa Raine.

00:03:16.977 --> 00:03:18.211
Well...

00:03:18.211 --> 00:03:20.981
...I never thought you'd be in the
business of collecting rewards.

00:03:20.981 --> 00:03:24.178
I had heard there were
people in that business.

00:03:27.187 --> 00:03:28.588
Rosa Raine...

00:03:28.588 --> 00:03:32.826
...27-years-old, high-ranking
officer in the German Red Army.

00:03:32.826 --> 00:03:34.589
Although an heiress to the
Raine financial group...

00:03:35.061 --> 00:03:37.431
...she took part in bombing
Ramstein Airforce Base...

00:03:37.431 --> 00:03:39.433
...and in 7 other terrorist incidents.

00:03:39.433 --> 00:03:41.368
She's the most wanted
woman on the list.

00:03:41.368 --> 00:03:44.838
She's certainly a
great target for us...

00:03:44.838 --> 00:03:46.773
...but don't you think
it's a bit dangerous...

00:03:46.773 --> 00:03:50.004
...for an insurance investigator
to be getting involved?

00:03:52.979 --> 00:03:55.345
I can see that Rosa is a terrorist.

00:03:55.549 --> 00:03:59.713
But now she's fed up with the violence
and is willing to turn herself in.

00:04:01.822 --> 00:04:05.826
Are you saying that she's
asking her family for help?

00:04:05.826 --> 00:04:06.690
Yes.

00:04:06.893 --> 00:04:10.329
Lloyd's has close ties to
the Raine Financial Group.

00:04:10.597 --> 00:04:11.898
Regardless...

00:04:11.898 --> 00:04:14.765
...we'll catch her within a week.

00:04:15.101 --> 00:04:16.703
Under German law...

00:04:16.703 --> 00:04:20.503
...the sentence is lighter
when one turns oneself in.

00:04:21.141 --> 00:04:23.877
There's 5 million
marks on her head!

00:04:23.877 --> 00:04:25.145
Not only Rosa!

00:04:25.145 --> 00:04:26.880
There should also be
Thomas Mueller...

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.682
...and Augusto Atcar
at their hideout.

00:04:28.682 --> 00:04:34.052
We have a report that
they're with the ringleader.

00:04:34.788 --> 00:04:35.777
The ringleader?

00:04:35.989 --> 00:04:38.325
If she were to disappear...

00:04:38.325 --> 00:04:40.126
...they'll flee their hideout...

00:04:40.126 --> 00:04:43.997
...and we'll lose a million marks.

00:04:43.997 --> 00:04:47.228
You wanted to locate their
hideout and arrest them together?

00:04:47.901 --> 00:04:49.669
Amateur...

00:04:49.669 --> 00:04:52.405
We don't have the authority
to arrest anyone.

00:04:52.405 --> 00:04:56.603
We'll just flush them out and
report them to the authorities.

00:04:58.311 --> 00:05:00.836
We'd like you to stay out of it.

00:05:01.314 --> 00:05:05.352
So you're saying that
there's no role for me.

00:05:05.352 --> 00:05:06.286
Of course not!

00:05:06.286 --> 00:05:09.589
We're dealing with a
professional terrorist here.

00:05:09.589 --> 00:05:13.218
You don't look like one who
can handle this violent world.

00:05:14.427 --> 00:05:15.860
I understand.

00:05:16.029 --> 00:05:18.429
I'll leave for today.

00:05:18.765 --> 00:05:21.165
Hey, what do you
mean, "for today"?!

00:05:23.603 --> 00:05:26.106
Impressive monitoring equipment.

00:05:26.106 --> 00:05:28.308
Are there seven in all...

00:05:28.308 --> 00:05:29.707
...or are there eight?

00:05:32.379 --> 00:05:36.149
I can see why you're so
eager about the prize.

00:05:36.149 --> 00:05:36.877
So long.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:43.089
John, keep an eye on him.

00:05:43.089 --> 00:05:45.557
Huh? You think it's worth
watching that nobody?

00:05:46.159 --> 00:05:50.425
We don't want that "nobody"
to interfere with us.

00:06:03.643 --> 00:06:06.510
I've spotted Thomas Mueller.

00:06:06.646 --> 00:06:07.977
I'm on his trail.

00:06:24.731 --> 00:06:27.133
He suspects he's being trailed.

00:06:27.133 --> 00:06:30.068
He took the down
escalator after going up.

00:06:30.203 --> 00:06:31.761
Wish you luck, Walter.

00:06:44.884 --> 00:06:46.476
It's Augusto Atcar!

00:06:47.153 --> 00:06:49.289
With Rosa, Mueller, Hoffman...

00:06:49.289 --> 00:06:50.551
We have all four.

00:06:51.424 --> 00:06:52.592
This is Michael.

00:06:52.592 --> 00:06:53.456
Acknowledged.

00:06:54.194 --> 00:06:55.957
Walter here. Roger that.

00:06:56.429 --> 00:06:59.489
No question that's their hideout.

00:06:59.833 --> 00:07:02.063
Just one left to go.

00:07:02.469 --> 00:07:04.596
Just be careful.

00:07:04.938 --> 00:07:05.836
I know.

00:07:11.911 --> 00:07:13.208
That guy!

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:15.447
What happened, Walter?

00:07:15.682 --> 00:07:16.750
It's Keaton!

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:18.318
He's near the hideout!

00:07:18.318 --> 00:07:19.182
What?!

00:07:19.986 --> 00:07:21.613
John, can you hear me?

00:07:21.888 --> 00:07:23.014
Yes, sir!

00:07:23.156 --> 00:07:25.592
I thought you had
your eye on Keaton.

00:07:25.592 --> 00:07:27.321
Well, uh...

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:29.229
You lost him, huh?

00:07:29.229 --> 00:07:30.218
Yes.

00:07:30.497 --> 00:07:31.828
Why didn't you report?!

00:07:33.299 --> 00:07:34.857
I'm sorry.

00:07:35.502 --> 00:07:36.903
Save it.

00:07:36.903 --> 00:07:38.505
Get back to headquarters.

00:07:38.505 --> 00:07:39.472
Yes, sir.

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:51.209
Oh.

00:07:51.484 --> 00:07:54.942
Mr. Keaton, I'm very impressed.
Just magnificent.

00:07:57.991 --> 00:08:00.960
Losing us and then
trailing us instead.

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:03.520
Well done for an amateur.

00:08:03.997 --> 00:08:07.057
Aren't you the "Little Giant"?

00:08:07.333 --> 00:08:08.391
Huh?

00:08:08.768 --> 00:08:10.470
I remembered...

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:13.306
...that there was this
genius of an inspector...

00:08:13.306 --> 00:08:15.501
...called the "Little
Giant" at Scotland Yard.

00:08:16.076 --> 00:08:18.340
I believe his name was Pitock.

00:08:19.179 --> 00:08:23.240
I heard there was some trouble
7 years ago and he quit the job.

00:08:26.186 --> 00:08:28.484
So, what about it?

00:08:28.655 --> 00:08:31.783
Is that supposed to
weaken my position?

00:08:32.358 --> 00:08:33.347
Of course not.

00:08:34.060 --> 00:08:34.992
I just...

00:08:35.462 --> 00:08:39.365
...thought if you are
who I think you are...

00:08:39.365 --> 00:08:42.630
...the ringleader you're
after might be Heinz Becker.

00:08:44.337 --> 00:08:47.636
He's the very top among
the world's terrorists...

00:08:47.874 --> 00:08:50.877
...and the prize money is
at least one million marks.

00:08:50.877 --> 00:08:53.079
I don't have to answer you.

00:08:53.079 --> 00:08:55.070
You're wrong.

00:08:55.582 --> 00:08:58.518
We received a call today
from the Raine family.

00:08:58.518 --> 00:09:02.784
They fear she'll be
tortured for her betrayal.

00:09:03.590 --> 00:09:06.359
Do you know that Becker
has a nickname, too?

00:09:06.359 --> 00:09:08.623
Just as they used to call
you the "Little Giant"?

00:09:09.295 --> 00:09:11.729
You mean the "hanging
judge" of the terrorists?

00:09:12.432 --> 00:09:14.798
Rosa will be killed
if he shows up.

00:09:15.668 --> 00:09:19.297
We'll call the authorities
before they can do that.

00:09:23.943 --> 00:09:27.606
Anyway, just stay away
from their hideout.

00:09:30.683 --> 00:09:31.618
Um...

00:09:31.618 --> 00:09:33.279
...one thing's bothering me.

00:09:33.553 --> 00:09:36.386
I noticed that there's a
weakness in your stake out.

00:09:37.557 --> 00:09:40.326
The clearing in the
back where Walter is.

00:09:40.326 --> 00:09:43.124
It's like he's asking to be seen.

00:09:44.097 --> 00:09:44.864
Oh?

00:09:44.864 --> 00:09:48.163
Think you can give
advice to a pro?

00:09:55.809 --> 00:09:57.510
All clear.

00:09:57.510 --> 00:10:00.604
When is that Becker
going to show up?

00:10:00.747 --> 00:10:03.307
He seems like a cautious fellow.

00:10:04.217 --> 00:10:06.276
Walter, how's everything going?

00:10:06.786 --> 00:10:10.119
I feel like taking a nap.

00:10:10.223 --> 00:10:12.125
Hang on, buddy.

00:10:12.125 --> 00:10:14.320
We'll send a replacement.

00:10:46.526 --> 00:10:48.585
B-Becker!

00:10:51.698 --> 00:10:52.926
It's Walter.

00:10:53.199 --> 00:10:54.723
Becker's got me.

00:10:55.001 --> 00:10:58.438
He'll free me if we don't
report this to the police.

00:10:58.438 --> 00:10:59.598
P-Please!

00:10:59.939 --> 00:11:01.907
Do as he says!

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:07.341
This came in at
14:15 from Walter.

00:11:08.047 --> 00:11:08.848
What should we do?

00:11:08.848 --> 00:11:13.217
They'll kill Walter even
if we do as they say!

00:11:13.987 --> 00:11:16.547
The only way is to
rescue him on our own.

00:11:17.257 --> 00:11:18.884
Right on, sir!

00:11:19.325 --> 00:11:20.493
Let's do it!

00:11:20.493 --> 00:11:21.761
We can do it,

00:11:21.761 --> 00:11:23.456
we're professionals.

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:27.233
John, go find a house that
we can do a simulation on.

00:11:27.233 --> 00:11:29.168
We need to do this right.

00:11:29.168 --> 00:11:29.998
Right, sir!

00:11:30.236 --> 00:11:32.405
The rest of you,
keep up the stakeout.

00:11:32.405 --> 00:11:33.303
Yes, sir!

00:11:35.942 --> 00:11:37.034
However...

00:11:38.278 --> 00:11:41.681
...we have to admit
that we're amateurs...

00:11:41.681 --> 00:11:43.342
...when it comes to terrorists.

00:12:07.607 --> 00:12:10.940
Twenty-four seconds
to secure it.

00:12:11.477 --> 00:12:13.001
Not bad.

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:16.149
Their hideout is
a two-story house.

00:12:16.149 --> 00:12:18.344
They change guard
every four hours.

00:12:19.919 --> 00:12:22.121
They all eat on the first floor.

00:12:22.121 --> 00:12:24.351
Expect one to keep watch
on the second floor.

00:12:24.857 --> 00:12:26.620
We should attack then.

00:12:28.294 --> 00:12:30.997
A professional who is
familiar with terrorists...

00:12:30.997 --> 00:12:33.900
...says there's one way to deal
with a terrorist hostage-taking.

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:36.636
That is to break the door
down with a shot gun...

00:12:36.636 --> 00:12:39.161
...and use tear gas.

00:12:47.814 --> 00:12:50.383
Some training you have here.

00:12:50.383 --> 00:12:52.010
You again.

00:12:52.151 --> 00:12:56.986
And what kind of advice are
you going to give us today?

00:12:58.891 --> 00:13:01.553
I want to help out.

00:13:02.662 --> 00:13:03.830
As we said!

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:07.391
Mr. Pitock doesn't work
with amateurs like you!

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:09.769
Rosa is also tied up.

00:13:09.769 --> 00:13:12.533
You checked their hideout?

00:13:12.605 --> 00:13:15.008
Let me hear your plans.

00:13:15.008 --> 00:13:17.135
How dare you, you bastard...!

00:13:17.276 --> 00:13:21.576
We're going in when they take
their meals on the first floor.

00:13:22.448 --> 00:13:23.813
Mr. Pitock!?

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:28.087
Then how about me climbing into
the second floor at the same time?

00:13:28.087 --> 00:13:29.489
But how?

00:13:29.489 --> 00:13:30.888
I'll manage somehow.

00:13:32.425 --> 00:13:34.494
You can help us, but...

00:13:34.494 --> 00:13:36.553
...promise me one thing.

00:13:36.863 --> 00:13:39.354
I want you to follow my orders.

00:13:41.667 --> 00:13:45.138
I'll tell you the real reason
that I left Scotland Yard.

00:13:45.138 --> 00:13:49.709
Seven years ago, in order to bust
a major drug deal going on...

00:13:49.709 --> 00:13:52.473
...I had staked out a disco in Soho.

00:13:53.279 --> 00:13:57.181
No guns were to be pulled
until the deal went down.

00:13:57.583 --> 00:14:01.383
Unfortunately, there was one
particular rookie on my team.

00:14:02.055 --> 00:14:05.547
He had a heart as
small as a rabbit's.

00:14:06.526 --> 00:14:08.194
I don't know what
came over him...

00:14:08.194 --> 00:14:11.322
...but he suddenly pulled
out his gun in the disco.

00:14:22.175 --> 00:14:25.044
The dealer got away...

00:14:25.044 --> 00:14:27.346
...and two officers...

00:14:27.346 --> 00:14:30.281
...and one patron lost their lives.

00:14:31.651 --> 00:14:35.488
From then on, I decided
not to work with amateurs.

00:14:35.488 --> 00:14:39.822
Amateurs can't judge the situation
well or stay patient for very long.

00:14:46.032 --> 00:14:49.001
We're going in tomorrow
at exactly at 8:00.

00:14:49.001 --> 00:14:51.704
We need five minutes to
secure the first floor.

00:14:51.704 --> 00:14:56.232
You go in to the second
floor one minute later.

00:14:58.111 --> 00:14:59.345
You bastard!

00:14:59.345 --> 00:15:00.937
How dare you!

00:15:01.547 --> 00:15:04.717
When you shoot at a
door with a shotgun...

00:15:04.717 --> 00:15:08.517
...you should aim at the
hinges, not the key hole.

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:14.026
Well, just to make sure...

00:15:14.026 --> 00:15:18.224
...I go in after the assault
has already begun, right?

00:15:20.133 --> 00:15:21.361
See you there.

00:15:23.202 --> 00:15:24.464
Oh, right.

00:15:24.837 --> 00:15:27.507
Just for your information...

00:15:27.507 --> 00:15:29.375
...Hoffman has a MP5...

00:15:29.375 --> 00:15:30.743
...Mueller, an UZI...

00:15:30.743 --> 00:15:32.578
...Atcar, a G3...

00:15:32.578 --> 00:15:35.206
...and Becker has a
sawed-off shotgun.

00:15:41.621 --> 00:15:42.588
Tonio!

00:15:42.588 --> 00:15:43.452
Yes, sir!

00:15:43.623 --> 00:15:47.260
Do a background
check on Keaton.

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:48.056
Yes, sir!

00:15:48.661 --> 00:15:52.098
Mr. Pitock, why
did you let him in?

00:15:52.098 --> 00:15:54.934
He may not simply be an amateur.

00:15:54.934 --> 00:15:58.304
He knew that you need at least
seven people for a stakeout.

00:15:58.304 --> 00:16:00.534
That's more than
you learn at school.

00:16:01.107 --> 00:16:03.598
He's familiar with guns
and breaking down doors.

00:16:04.043 --> 00:16:09.071
Well, I suppose we can
always use an extra hand.

00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:24.325
It's 7:50 and Keaton
is still not here.

00:16:24.864 --> 00:16:26.764
He probably chickened out.

00:16:33.372 --> 00:16:34.202
Darn.

00:16:34.674 --> 00:16:36.976
There's a maintenance
truck coming.

00:16:36.976 --> 00:16:38.244
What?

00:16:38.244 --> 00:16:39.845
According to the schedule...

00:16:39.845 --> 00:16:43.281
...there shouldn't be any
maintenance this way.

00:16:51.991 --> 00:16:53.359
It's Keaton.

00:16:53.359 --> 00:16:53.984
What?!

00:16:54.527 --> 00:16:55.895
Clever.

00:16:55.895 --> 00:16:58.363
That way he can charge
into the second floor.

00:16:58.831 --> 00:17:00.765
Okay, let's get started.

00:17:44.543 --> 00:17:45.378
That idiot!

00:17:45.378 --> 00:17:48.180
He was supposed to go
in one minute after us!

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:50.341
I bet he's in a panic.

00:17:50.783 --> 00:17:52.546
Are we calling off the operation?

00:17:52.718 --> 00:17:55.521
The hostages will be in
danger if they go up!

00:17:55.521 --> 00:17:57.011
We have no choice!

00:18:08.634 --> 00:18:09.862
Look for the stairs!

00:18:25.151 --> 00:18:27.415
Why are they still downstairs?

00:18:31.991 --> 00:18:34.293
Okay, Daniel. Let us down.

00:18:34.293 --> 00:18:36.796
Keaton, you fooled me.

00:18:36.796 --> 00:18:40.800
You didn't say it would
be a dangerous job!

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:44.327
You can give me hell later.
Just get us out of here!

00:18:44.603 --> 00:18:48.061
Don't worry, I'm getting out
of here as fast as I can.

00:19:14.266 --> 00:19:17.770
I heard that Rosa Raine
turned herself in.

00:19:17.770 --> 00:19:19.761
Yes, thanks to you.

00:19:22.141 --> 00:19:25.244
Professional soldiers
tend to retreat...

00:19:25.244 --> 00:19:27.046
...when they're faced
with a surprise attack.

00:19:27.046 --> 00:19:30.072
And they counterattack
after they first regroup.

00:19:30.516 --> 00:19:33.819
They stayed on the first floor...

00:19:33.819 --> 00:19:37.186
...because you took them by
surprise on the second floor.

00:19:37.590 --> 00:19:39.558
That's when we went in.

00:19:39.558 --> 00:19:42.194
Thinking they were surrounded...

00:19:42.194 --> 00:19:44.094
...they couldn't make a move.

00:19:46.799 --> 00:19:49.835
So, hitting the terrorists
from the first floor...

00:19:49.835 --> 00:19:53.239
...which was our original plan...

00:19:53.239 --> 00:19:55.298
...was a miscalculation.

00:19:56.208 --> 00:19:57.402
Isn't that right?

00:19:58.544 --> 00:20:01.012
I hear you received the reward.

00:20:02.381 --> 00:20:05.418
Yes, but they also gave
us a strict reprimand.

00:20:05.418 --> 00:20:06.986
That's terrible!

00:20:06.986 --> 00:20:08.654
You caught all the terrorists...

00:20:08.654 --> 00:20:11.589
Heroes who saved the
lives of the hostages!

00:20:33.879 --> 00:20:35.281
Are you all right?

00:20:35.281 --> 00:20:37.044
Yes, I'll manage.

00:20:37.249 --> 00:20:40.912
That Keaton is quite agile.

00:20:41.253 --> 00:20:43.122
He finished the guards off...

00:20:43.122 --> 00:20:45.613
...and got both me and the girl out.

00:20:45.858 --> 00:20:48.088
Who on earth is he?

00:20:49.061 --> 00:20:51.256
This just came today.

00:20:56.335 --> 00:20:58.701
Taichi Hiraga Keaton.

00:20:59.538 --> 00:21:01.207
Mother: English.

00:21:01.207 --> 00:21:02.868
Father: Japanese.

00:21:03.042 --> 00:21:05.010
He has British nationality.

00:21:05.811 --> 00:21:09.212
Graduated from Oxford
University in archaeology.

00:21:10.449 --> 00:21:13.543
After three years in the army...

00:21:13.719 --> 00:21:17.678
...he joined the Special
Air Service, or SAS.

00:21:18.324 --> 00:21:19.859
SAS!

00:21:19.859 --> 00:21:21.727
He is now out of the force...

00:21:21.727 --> 00:21:25.998
...but he performed supremely
well when he took part...

00:21:25.998 --> 00:21:28.592
...in the Iranian Embassy incident.

00:21:29.702 --> 00:21:30.870
In other words...

00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:36.331
...Keaton was the professional
and we were the amateurs.

00:21:53.926 --> 00:22:04.937
In a dream I had,
I noticed your distant, faint voice

00:22:04.937 --> 00:22:12.002
A scene so familiar
playing out in reality

00:22:12.845 --> 00:22:16.246
In my consciousness

00:22:17.116 --> 00:22:25.291
The sky I was searching for
brings forth a gentleness

00:22:25.291 --> 00:22:29.227
Time will give me the answer

00:22:35.534 --> 00:22:40.873
In the blank scene before me

00:22:40.873 --> 00:22:46.745
I walk as the wind blows

00:22:46.745 --> 00:22:54.019
I just want to touch
it with my own hands

00:22:54.019 --> 00:23:01.391
As the wind blows against me

00:23:08.567 --> 00:23:09.735
Reminiscences.

00:23:09.735 --> 00:23:13.193
Memories are reflected upon
with warmth, fun, and fondness.

00:23:14.139 --> 00:23:16.375
The enchanting stare of a young girl.

00:23:16.375 --> 00:23:18.400
Is it sincere?

00:23:19.278 --> 00:23:23.015
People live their daily lives wearing
masks that hide their true selves.

00:23:23.015 --> 00:23:25.551
To friends, siblings, parents...

00:23:25.551 --> 00:23:28.821
...and even to their spouses
to whom they swore fidelity.

00:23:28.821 --> 00:23:30.189
Strange Tale of Lasagna

00:23:30.189 --> 00:23:32.491
Strange Tale of Lasagna
Next time... Strange Tale of Lasagna

00:23:32.491 --> 00:23:35.085
Strange Tale of Lasagna
